<title>USA: Wall Street stocks mixed in early trade, Dow up.</title>
<headline>Wall Street stocks mixed in early trade, Dow up.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wall Street stocks opened mixed on Thursday after Wednesday's sell-off, with the Dow Industrials seeing at least a temporary bounce at the open.</p>
<p>--Dow Industrials  .DJI up eight at 6755.</p>
<p>--Nasdaq Composite  .IXIC up three at 1351.</p>
<p>--S&amp;P Index  .SPX up fractionally at 778.</p>
<p>--NYSE advance/decline  .AD.N 261/293</p>
<p>--Nasdaq advance/decline  .AD.O 606/448</p>
<p>--The 30-year long bond down 4/32 to yield 6.77 percent.</p>
<p>-- Wall Street desk, 212-859-1720</p>
</text>
